\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {1}Can the geometry of a healthy coronary tree tell us who will develop plaque?}{1}{section.1}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The reasoning behind the research question. Steps 1 to 4 concern where in a single coronary tree plaque forms, and each rests on published work. Step 5 is also documented, but step 6, whether the shape of a healthy tree predicts who develops plaque, has not been tested.}}{1}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rq-chain}{{1}{1}{The reasoning behind the research question. Steps 1 to 4 concern where in a single coronary tree plaque forms, and each rests on published work. Step 5 is also documented, but step 6, whether the shape of a healthy tree predicts who develops plaque, has not been tested}{figure.1}{}}
