\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The tortuosity index cannot tell these three vessels apart, but curvature can. Each synthetic centerline is 50\,mm long between ends 40\,mm apart, so all three share the tortuosity index $\tau = 1.25$, yet their mean curvature differs sixfold. Color shows local curvature $\kappa $, the inverse of the radius of the bend at each point. Curvature, not $\tau $, tracked low shear in 127 patients \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {kashyap2022tortuosity}.}}{3}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rq-curvature}{{3}{3}{The tortuosity index cannot tell these three vessels apart, but curvature can. Each synthetic centerline is 50\,mm long between ends 40\,mm apart, so all three share the tortuosity index $\tau = 1.25$, yet their mean curvature differs sixfold. Color shows local curvature $\kappa $, the inverse of the radius of the bend at each point. Curvature, not $\tau $, tracked low shear in 127 patients \cite {kashyap2022tortuosity}}{figure.3}{}}
